## 1.1 Programming Paradigm

Definition

A Programming Paradigm is a style or approach of writing and organizing code
to solve a problem.

Different paradigms solve the same problem in different ways.

Real-Life Example

Suppose you want to travel from Mumbai to Delhi.
You can travel by:
✈️ Flight
🚆 Train
🚌 Bus

The destination is the same.
Only the method of traveling is different.

Similarly, in programming, different ways of solving a problem are called
Programming Paradigms.

1.1 Types of Programming Paradigms
   Some common programming paradigms are:
   1. Procedural Programming
   2. Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
   1. Functional Programming
   2. Logic Programming

For learning Java OOP, we will focus primarily on procedural programming
and object-oriented programming.


