# 6. Class Naming Conventions in Java

Following proper naming conventions improves readability and follows Java
standards.
Naming Convention for Class and Object

✅ 1. Class Name Should Start with an Uppercase Letter
Correct: Student, Bank
Incorrect: student, bank

✅ 2. Use Upper Camel Case (Pascal Case) for Multi-Word Class Names
Correct: BankController, StudentDetails
Incorrect: bankcontroller, studentdetails, student_details

✅ 3. The Class Name Should Be Descriptive
It should give an idea of what the class does.
Correct: CustomerAccount, OrderManager
Incorrect: Xyz, Temp

✅ 4. The Class Name Should Be a Noun
Since a class represents an entity or object, it should be a noun.
Correct: Car, Employee, Invoice

These are actions (verbs) and should be used as method names.

